        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "June 2026 BEA disposable personal income first-print forecast"
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "The target is BEA NIPA Table 2.6 disposable personal income, account A067RC / DSPI: monthly, seasonally adjusted annual rate, in billions of dollars. Resolution is the June first print only; the retained ledger ALFRED URL has a May-2026 vintage-date discrepancy, but the target and its first-print policy remain unchanged."
        },
        {
          "kind": "tool",
          "tool": "official.lookup",
          "call": "Checked BEA's June 25 Personal Income and Outlays release for the latest DPI outcome and contributors.",
          "result": "BEA reported that May disposable personal income increased $164.9 billion, or 0.7 percent; personal income rose $181.6 billion and personal saving was $704.2 billion."
        },
        {
          "kind": "tool",
          "tool": "official.lookup",
          "call": "Checked the BEA release schedule entry and cross-checked the immediately preceding official release.",
          "result": "BEA schedules Personal Income and Outlays, June 2026 for July 30 at 8:30 a.m.; the preceding May release reported current-dollar DPI growth of 0.7 percent and real DPI growth of 0.3 percent."
        },
        {
          "kind": "tool",
          "tool": "official.lookup",
          "call": "Fetched the DSPI history mirror for the same monthly SAAR series and account code.",
          "result": "The BEA-sourced DSPI series shows May 2026 23,651.7, April 23,486.9, March 23,510.4, February 23,382.4, and January 23,395.9 billion dollars SAAR; it identifies BEA account code A067RC."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Reference class/base rate: recent successive DSPI changes are +164.8, -23.5, +128.0, and -13.5 billion dollars. May is above this short reference class and BEA attributes part of the wider personal-income increase to a second round of Supplemental Disaster Relief Program payments, so I do not extrapolate its full change."
        },
        {
          "kind": "math",
          "text": "Prior/update/interval: persistence prior is the mean of the four fetched January-to-May successive DSPI changes, +64.0 billion dollars; historical sample is those four changes. Their sample sigma = 96.5 billion dollars, so 1.28*sigma = 123.5 billion dollars for an 80% half-width. I update the +64.0 prior modestly to +68.3 for continuing compensation and nominal-price growth, while allowing May's farm-payment component to fade: 23,651.7 + 68.3 = 23,720.0; 23,720.0 \u00b1 123.5 gives 23,596.5 to 23,843.5."
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Counter-consideration: upside risk is another unusually large transfer or farm-proprietor payment, which would land above the interval. downside risk is a reversal of May's temporary income support or weak compensation; a decline exceeding roughly $55 billion from May would land below the interval."
        },
        {
          "kind": "forecast",
          "point": 23720.0,
          "ciLow": 23596.5,
          "ciHigh": 23843.5
        }
